{"name":"Nocturnal Flight","hex":"#675754","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nocturnal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person, creature, group, or species, primarily active during the night.","Of an occurrence, taking place at night, nightly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or creature that is active at night.","A device for telling the time at night, rather like a sundial but read according to the stars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nocturnal"},{"term":"flight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of flying; the ability to fly.","An instance of flying."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fast, swift, fleet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nocturnal animal","blocks":[{"text":"Nocturnality is a behavior in some non-human animals characterized by being active during the night and sleeping during the day. The common adjective is nocturnal, with diurnal meaning the opposite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Owl_at_Night.jpg/330px-Owl_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nocturnal_animal","wikidata":"Q309179"},{"title":"Flight","blocks":[{"text":"Flight or flying is the motion of an object through an atmosphere or through the vacuum of space, in this case also called spaceflight, without contacting any planetary surface. This can be achieved by generating aerodynamic lift associated with gliding or propulsive thrust, aerostatically using buoyancy, or by ballistic movement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Juvenile_pelecanus_occidentalis_in_flight.jpg/330px-Juvenile_pelecanus_occidentalis_in_flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flight","wikidata":"Q206021"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.w